      "note": "<p>PROVISIONAL Codex English-first proposal. Supplied subjects, articles and auxiliaries remain unwrapped: <i>they</i>, <i>have</i>, <i>must</i>, <i>there is</i>, <i>could ever be</i>, <i>To do this they give the following</i>, <i>It is</i>, <i>which the consciousness has to grasp to</i>, and <i>look at</i> are not assigned as independent lexical equivalents. The first <code>rnam shes</code> belongs to the first English <i>consciousness</i>; the occurrence in the seed clause is banked once at the earlier of its two explanatory English realizations, while <code>rang gi</code> selects the later <i>itself</i>. All four <code>sogs</code> occurrences are resolved separately as the licensed closing gestures <i>and so on</i>, <i>and so on</i>, <i>and the rest</i>, and <i>or whatever</i>.</p><p>The eye-faculty, five-faculty, and five-consciousness compounds retain only strictly contained members. Passive <i>was</i> around <i>planted</i>, causal framing around <i>ripening</i>, and supplied <i>physical</i> before <i>objects</i> stay outside the lexical spans. The final Tibetan conclusion beginning <code>de'i phyir</code> restates the absence of outer objects separately from consciousness but has no remaining continuous English exponent after the preceding explanatory recast, so it is omitted rather than falsely nulled or attached to an earlier repeated phrase.</p><p>The appended Selection Two heading is the registered following-heading glue class and is left unwrapped; no new erratum is proposed. No source wording or binding <code>hgm_gloss</code> was changed.</p>"
